  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Ice Pikmin freeze enemies on contact, making them safe to swarm with fragile Pikmin types—always lead with 3–5 Ice Pikmin against flying enemies to ground them before committing your full squad.",
      "Oatchi charges deal massive stagger damage and can be chained: charge → retrieve → recharge takes 8 seconds per cycle, providing reliable stagger control against armoured enemies without losing Pikmin.",
      "The Dandori scoring system rewards parallel task completion—assign Pikmin to carrying objects while simultaneously commanding Oatchi to fight enemies. True S-rank Dandori requires zero idle time from any squad member.",
      "Night expeditions unlock Glow Pikmin, which cannot be carried back to base—use them exclusively for combat and never waste them on carrying tasks that can wait for daytime.",
      "Caves reset their internal day timer when you exit and re-enter—if you leave a cave with high-value items uncollected, those items remain but you lose the time invested reaching them. Plan cave runs to completion."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "氷ピクミンは接触で敵を凍らせるため、脆いピクミン種類を群がらせる前に3〜5匹の氷ピクミンで空飛ぶ敵を地面に落とす。",
      "オッチンの突進は大きなひるみダメージを与えてチェーンできる。突進→回収→再チャージが1サイクル8秒。装甲敵に対して安定したひるみ制御ができ、ピクミンを失わない。",
      "ダンドリスコアは並行タスク完了を評価する。ピクミンにオブジェクトを運ばせながら、同時にオッチンを敵と戦わせる。真のSランクは全隊員のアイドル時間をゼロにする必要がある。",
      "夜の探索でヒカリピクミンが解放されるが、基地に持ち帰れない。戦闘専用として使い、昼間に待てる運搬タスクには絶対に使わない。",
      "ドルフィン号に帰還して洞窟に再入場すると内部の時計がリセットされる。高価値アイテムを未収集のまま出ると、アイテムは残るが到達までの時間投資が無駄になる。洞窟は完遂計画で入る。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "First Day Pikmin Squad Building",
        "body": "On day 1, focus entirely on Red and Yellow Pikmin production—Red for combat durability, Yellow for bomb-weight utility and electrical hazard immunity. Do not unlock Winged Pikmin until you have a stable base squad of 60+ Pikmin; Winged Pikmin are fast but fragile and best used for precision tasks rather than mass combat. The first cave (Burrow of Beginnings) is designed to teach Pikmin juggling: bring 20 Red, 15 Yellow, 10 Rock Pikmin and leave the rest at base."
      },
      {
        "title": "Rescue Pup Introduction and Oatchi Upgrades",
        "body": "Oatchi's first three upgrades should be: Buff (carry weight +5), Rush (charge damage +50%), and Heal (emergency Pikmin revival 3× per day). These three fundamentals cover the combat-carry-survival triad that defines efficient early play. Delaying Buff in favour of attack upgrades means each carry trip to base requires more round trips, costing 15–20 minutes per day of Dandori time over the first five in-game days."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Dandori Battle Mastery",
        "body": "Dandori Battles require defeating the opponent's Pikmin output while simultaneously outscoring them. The most efficient Dandori Battle strategy: prioritise high-value objects (large fruit, pots) in the first 60 seconds before the opponent can deploy defensive Pikmin. Use Bomb Rocks aggressively in the final 30 seconds to clear enemy Pikmin carrying objects near their base—the object resets to neutral, giving you extra scoring opportunities."
      },
      {
        "title": "Night Expedition Glow Strategy",
        "body": "Night expeditions feature Lumiknolls that spawn Gloom enemies. Glow Pikmin recharge at Lumiknolls—position your Glow squad at 50% health near the Lumiknoll before a Gloom enemy wave rather than fighting from full health on the open field. The Lumiknoll recharge triggers automatically when Glow Pikmin touch the base; use this as a healing loop by sending injured Glow Pikmin back after each wave rather than keeping them engaged continuously."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Olimar's Shipwreck Tale",
        "body": "Olimar's Shipwreck Tale unlocks after finishing the main story and replays the game from Olimar's perspective with new dialogue and item placements. This mode restricts you to classic Pikmin types (no Ice or Glow) and features remixed cave layouts. The most important adjustment: Rock Pikmin replace Ice Pikmin for crowd control—use Rock to stagger armoured enemies rather than attempting to burn through their armour. The challenge is completing the same maps within stricter Dandori time windows."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Carrying only one Pikmin type into caves—most caves require at least 3 types to cover fire, water, and electrical hazards simultaneously; entering with a single-type squad creates forced retreats.",
      "Letting Pikmin idle at base while exploring solo—idle Pikmin produce nothing; assign them to carrying sprouts from onion to base, watering flowers, or collecting nearby small items even when not in your active area.",
      "Charging Oatchi into groups with explosive enemies present—bomb enemies detonate when hit by Oatchi's charge, dealing friendly-fire damage to surrounding Pikmin; target non-explosive enemies first.",
      "Spending Sparklium on non-Oatchi upgrades before maxing Buff—carry weight is multiplicative on Dandori efficiency; each Buff upgrade saves more time per day than any combat upgrade provides.",
      "Leaving rare Pikmin types (Purple, White) in active squad during transit—Purple and White Pikmin cannot be found in this game without specific items; losing them to ambient hazards while walking is the most frustrating recovery grind."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "洞窟に1種類のピクミンだけ持って行く。多くの洞窟は炎・水・電気の危険に同時対応するため3種類以上必要。単一種での入洞は強制撤退を招く。",
      "探索中にピクミンを基地でアイドルにしておく。アイドルピクミンは何も生産しない。自分がいないエリアでも、オニオンからの芽の運搬、花の水やり、近くの小アイテム回収を割り当てる。",
      "爆発する敵がいる群れにオッチンを突進させる。爆弾持ちの敵はオッチンの突進で起爆し、周囲のピクミンに友軍誤射ダメージを与える。爆発しない敵から先に倒す。",
      "オッチンの「力持ち」を最大化する前にスパークリウムを他の強化に使う。運搬重量はダンドリ効率に乗算的に影響する。力持ちの強化は毎日の時間節約で、どの戦闘強化よりも価値が高い。",
      "レアピクミン（紫・白）を移動中に先頭に立たせる。紫・白ピクミンは特定アイテムなしで入手できない。周囲の危険で失うと最も回収が辛いグラインドになる。"
    ]
